*=======================================================================
* O2 Dyson orbitals for HERMES  —  Stage 1 of Paper/CASSCF/PLAN.md
*
* Produces the exact Kallen-Lehmann ingredients for
*     G_rs = SUM_n  d_r^n d_s^n / (E_F - IP_n)
* namely the Dyson orbitals (weights) and the exact IPs (poles), for the
* single O-O pair.
*
* O2 is the minimal multireference test: X 3Sigma_g- with two singly
* occupied degenerate pi* orbitals.  It is the small-molecule analogue of
* the near-degenerate beta frontier that made final_O2_doublet cost 32 h
* of QC-SCF (beta gap 0.000 +/- 0.005 Ha over all 105 samples).
*
* Active space CAS(12,8): 16 electrons total, 4 in the two O 1s core
* orbitals (Inactive=2), leaving 12 valence electrons in the 8 valence
* orbitals 2sig_g 2sig_u 3sig_g 1pi_u(x2) 1pi_g(x2) 3sig_u.
*
* group=c1 is REQUIRED, not cosmetic: HERMES needs a fixed, desymmetrised
* AO ordering, and the paper's benzene reference is likewise run in C1.
*
* JOB001 MUST be the neutral.  RASSI's Dyson loop runs JSTATE=1..DYSEXPSF
* over initial states and ISTATE=JSTATE+1..NSTATE over final states
* (src/rassi/writedys.f), so the N-electron state has to come first.
*=======================================================================

&GATEWAY
  coord  = o2.xyz
  basis  = def2-SVP
  group  = c1

&SEWARD

*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* N-electron reference:  O2 neutral,  X 3Sigma_g-
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
&RASSCF
  Title    = O2 neutral triplet CAS(12,8)
  Spin     = 3
  Charge   = 0
  nActEl   = 12 0 0
  Inactive = 2
  Ras2     = 8
  CIRoot   = 1 1 1

* Natural orbitals of the N-electron reference define the NAO basis.
* NOTE their occupations are FRACTIONAL — see PLAN.md section 5.1.
>>COPY $Project.rasscf.molden  o2_neutral.rasscf.molden
>>COPY $Project.JobIph         JOB001

&CASPT2
  Title      = CASPT2 on the neutral reference
  Multistate = 1 1
  Imaginary  = 0.1

*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* (N-1)-electron final states:  O2+ doublets  (X 2Pi_g and above)
* Six roots give six poles.  The pole count is the summation-window
* problem of sec:benzene_window in another guise — argue it by
* convergence, not assertion.
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
&RASSCF
  Title    = O2+ doublet CAS(11,8), 6 roots
  Spin     = 2
  Charge   = 1
  nActEl   = 11 0 0
  Inactive = 2
  Ras2     = 8
  CIRoot   = 6 6 1

>>COPY $Project.JobIph  JOB002

&CASPT2
  Title      = MS-CASPT2 on the cation doublets
  Multistate = 6 1 2 3 4 5 6
  Imaginary  = 0.1

*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* (N-1)-electron final states:  O2+ quartets
* Removing one electron from a triplet reaches both doublet and quartet
* cations; omitting the quartets would truncate the pole spectrum on a
* spin selection rule rather than on convergence.
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
&RASSCF
  Title    = O2+ quartet CAS(11,8), 4 roots
  Spin     = 4
  Charge   = 1
  nActEl   = 11 0 0
  Inactive = 2
  Ras2     = 8
  CIRoot   = 4 4 1

>>COPY $Project.JobIph  JOB003

&CASPT2
  Title      = MS-CASPT2 on the cation quartets
  Multistate = 4 1 2 3 4
  Imaginary  = 0.1

*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Dyson orbitals and amplitudes.
*
* DYSExport = 1 0  ->  export for the first spin-free initial state (the
* neutral) and no spin-orbit states.  Writes Dyson.SF.molden.1 as a
* standard Molden file: [ATOMS], [GTO], [5D], [MO] with Ene=/Occup=.
*
* Reading that file: the coefficients are the UN-NORMALISED Dyson
* orbitals whose squared norm IS the pole strength
* (src/rassi/mkdysorb.f:117, DYSAMP = SQRT(sum OVLP^2)).  Do not
* normalise them on read — that silently deletes the spectral weights.
*
* Do NOT take the poles from the Molden Ene= field: molden_dysorb.f:814
* writes it as F10.4, truncating at 1e-4 Ha.  Take the state energies
* from this output at full precision and difference them.
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
&RASSI
  NrOfJobIphs = 3  1 6 4
  1
  1 2 3 4 5 6
  1 2 3 4
  DYSOn
  DYSExport
  1 0
